ey're called  projections for a reason we have to wait  for these individual counties in the  Secretary of State in every state of the  Union to actually certify the election  that takes three four five sometimes  seven days to get done because you have  to count absentee ballots from the  military you have to come absentee  ballot some diplomats absentee ballots  of citizens abroad provisional ballots  and that takes some time so instead of  us rushing this process which I've seen  a lot of folks push us to do including  the president why don't you let these  votes just get counted that is what  democracy is about eight counting votes  it takes  and now listen a lot of people are  wondering what's going on in Arizona  every state is allowed to run these  things within certain parameters the way  that they want to I mean they all have  different you know state statutes and  that kind of thing  in Arizona the fact that it's taking lot  is so long really not that unusual  The Washington Post writes about this  and says state law requires the envelope  these day know because so many people  vote by mail in Arizona the envelope to  be sealed inside and for elections  officials to match each signature to the  one on file with the voters registration  before even opening the envelope in this  election that's about 1.7 million  individual signatures that had to be  confirmed one by one total of about 2.3  million votes were cast in Arizona and  Jason the new totals tonight continued  to tech cinéma up the Democratic  challenger there any path you see for  McSally at this point the Republican  it's it's looking tough for the  Republicans out in Arizona but I don't  think the there's as much suspicion  about the process going on out there is  there is backe strictly down in Florida  I mean we know that some Democrats have  trouble accepting that they've lost  elections we saw this in 2016 it looks  like it's continued earlier this week  but I think the Republicans particularly  in South Florida in Broward County have  reason to be suspicious the election  supervisor there has been repeatedly  reprimanded by judges for destroying  ballots illegally counting bail other  ballots in secret and the real question  is whether the Democrats that are going  in going down there right now are there  because of valid integrity or there to  change the outcome of the election and I  and I think that Republicans are right  to be skeptical the process now I want  to make sure that we've spent some time  on Florida and get all of you to weigh  in on this so I will ask you to move a  little bit briskly Brad I want to start  with you  mark liest who is the attorney who  represents a number of Democrats in the  in is a household name to a lot of  people in these races and in these  fights in court he says this breaking as  provisional ballots are counted and  counties canvass the margin in Florida  Senate race has fallen under 15,000 I  expect the margin to tighten further in  advance of tomorrow's noon deadline and  as I said before this is a jump ball  going into the recount Brad which could  be triggered as soon as 3 o'clock  tomorrow it could but  there's something very suspicious than  in 67 counties in Florida whenever  there's a problem it always comes down  to the Democratic strongholds of Broward  and Palm Beach County I witnessed it  firsthand the governor had to bring a  lawsuit in order to get his people in  there to over to conduct some oversight  we had to do the same thing in the  Florida recount in 2000 there were  ballots found in 2000 trunks of cars and  in in hallways and and the ballot  security was it was non-existent so the  integrity is a question here because  they brought up integrity on Brad  because the FDLE the Florida Department  of Law Enforcement for the lawn for  somebody for the state of Florida has  already looked into this and said they  see no evidence of guys just so people  know there have been two rulings today  that seem to benefit the Scott campaign  at this point because there is you there  are state statutes here in play and  reporting and transparency are that you  know that needs to be now Jason Jason I  want to give you a final word in here  too because bill scher an attorney who's  dealt with a number of these problems in  Broward County says he's been filing  lawsuits against Brenda Snipes ever  since she was appointed for voting  irregularities in Broward County  Brenda Snipes in her election apparatus  caused everybody to have doubts about  where these votes are how many are left  and Jason that's not fair to the left or  the right Republicans or Democrats or  anybody else who voted right now there  there are problems with this election  supervisor it's a track record of  shenanigans down there and yes everyone  knows that the all the votes should be  counted but we need consistent rules to  make sure all of the votes are counted  the right way and consistently and  fairly on both sides and again  Republicans have reason to be suspicious  Democrats we're gonna run out of time  we're gonna run out of time but listen  we know that there are many other court  orders that have come out tonight that  are going to kick in tomorrow and and  listen we know this is far far from over  but I appreciate Jason's use of the word  shenanigan because it's underutilized in  my opinion Richard Jason at Brad thank  you all very much

